cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ClauseGate: Interpretable Verification of LLM Agent Tool Calls via Tri-Graph Tsetlin Machines with SAT-Verifiable Receipts and Counterfactual Argument Recourse"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anwar
    affiliation: "University of Agder (UiA)"
abstract: >
  A symbolic verification layer for any LLM-driven autonomous agent or
  MCP-style tool host. ClauseGate ingests the agent's proposed tool call,
  retrieved RAG context, and operator policy, builds a typed-edge
  multigraph, and emits an ALLOW / DENY / NEEDS-OVERSIGHT verdict together
  with the firing Boolean clauses, a SAT-verifiable signed receipt, and a
  counterfactual minimal-argument-edit that would flip the decision. The
  pipeline composes the Hierarchical Graph Tsetlin Machine and CUDA kernels
  from graphtm-cbr, the SAT receipt machinery from clauseguard, and the
  structural-distillation primitive from attention-distilled-graphtm.
  Targets EU AI Act Article 14 (human oversight) + Article 15
  (robustness/cybersecurity), OWASP LLM01:2025 (Prompt Injection), MITRE
  ATLAS AML.T0051/T0054/T0096, and NIST AI 600-1 (interpretability +
  confabulation) for any agentic system handling untrusted inputs.
date-released: 2026-05-24
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Tsetlin Machine
  - Graph Tsetlin Machine
  - Hierarchical Tsetlin Machine
  - LLM agent safety
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - tool-call verification
  - prompt injection
  - interpretable AI
  - SAT verification
  - counterfactual recourse
  - EU AI Act
  - OWASP LLM Top 10
  - MITRE ATLAS
  - neuro-symbolic
